{
 "about": "Headings read off the textbook pages by hand, 2026-09-22, to measure scripts/build_taxonomy.py. Three or more chapters per subject family, spread over classes 6-10 and over the book designs (numbered old books, numbered new books, unnumbered new Social Science, Class 10 History/Political Science/Economics). A topic is the book's first heading level inside a chapter, a subtopic its second. Not counted as headings: boxes and panels (Know a scientist, DON'T MISS OUT, Math Talk), activities, figures, tables, exercises, 'Summary'/'Before we move on' end matter, and a third, smaller heading level (Ganita Prakash 13pt black 'Idli-Vada Game'; Exploration's bold organelle names; hees101's 14pt italic 'Renewable resources'). A subtopic is matched together with its parent topic, so a right name under the wrong topic counts as wrong. The first eleven chapters were read while the extractor was being built on the same books, so their numbers are not independent; the three marked heldOut were read and written down before the extractor was run on them, and are reported separately. First run on the held-out three, before any change prompted by them: Maths 13/13 correct of 13 extracted against 14 true once 'Kite' is counted; Science 10/10 and 10/10; Social Science 9/9 extracted correct but only 9/15 found -- the subtopic level was lost to a 15.43pt vs 15pt size split (fixed by clustering sizes within 0.6pt).",
